{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And Cain went out.</b> He went out in submission, as though stealing the mind of the Most High." "<b>In the land of Nod.</b> In the land where all the exiles wander (נָדִים) there." "<b>East of Eden.</b> There his father was exiled when he was driven from the Garden of Eden, as it says ״וַיַּשְׁכֵּן מִקֶּדֶם לְגַן עֵדֶן״ — to guard the way of the entrance to the Garden, from which one may infer that Adam was there. And we find that an east wind gathers in every place the murderers, as it says ״אָז יַבְדִּיל מֹשֶׁה״ and so forth, ״מִזְרְחָה שָׁמֶשׁ״ (Deuteronomy 4). Another matter — בְּאֶרֶץ נוֹד: every place he went, the earth would quake beneath him, and the creatures would say, 'Depart from him — this is the one who killed his brother.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {2 "Rashi implicitly cites Genesis 3:24 (וישכן מקדם לגן עדן) and Deuteronomy 4:41–43 (אז יבדיל משה), where Moses designates cities of refuge 'toward the sunrise' (מזרחה שמש); the east-wind / eastward association with refuge for killers is the link."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:35.600124733Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}